  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Sofia Li in San Antonio with a zip code of 78260. She wants to exchange her digital camera because the zoom isn't sufficient for her bird-watching needs. She wants the maximum zoom capacity, same specs otherwise, and to use PayPal for any extra payment. First, I need to authenticate her. The previous step used find_user_id_by_name_zip and got user ID sofia_li_9219. Now, I should get her order details to check the status.\n\nSo, next step: Use get_user_details with user_id sofia_li_9219 to find her orders. Then, identify which order has the camera in question. Once the order is located, check its status. If it's delivered, proceed with exchange_delivered_order_items. She mentioned the exchange needs to be as soon as possible, so I need to find the correct item IDs for the current camera and the new one with max zoom. Also, ensure the new item is the same product type but with higher zoom. Since price isn't an issue, any difference will be covered by her PayPal. Need to confirm all details with her before proceeding.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"sofia_li_9219\"}}\n",
